 ],
 "notes": "Photos show: a single-storey brick base (double hollow brick, ~4.6 m) wrapping the whole plan with big sliding-glass openings and a recessed, canopied entrance on the street (south) side; above it a tall hall volume clad in translucent polycarbonate (milky white-blue) on the west/north, with a brick-faced upper block at the east end; flat, thin roof edge; blue court and pitch to the north, a ramp up to a north door, pollarded street trees. Interior (steel trusses, polycarbonate clerestory, blue floor) not modelled. Guessed: plan size (~44x24 m base, footprint area 1,914 m2 from ArchDaily), heights, which end the brick block is, ramp position, orientation. Aerial photo suggests the hall is at the street corner; placement approximate. Rounds 2-3: hall raised to ~2.7x the base as in the street photos, east brick block raised to match, shallow mono-pitch zinc roof added over the hall (photo of the corner shows a sloping top edge)."
